## Part 7: Phased Execution Roadmap

### Phase 1 — Foundation (CSS Design System)
Write `CSS/styles.css` from scratch: all tokens, typography, layout utilities, button variants, card styles.

### Phase 2 — Header, Hero, Trust Bar
Sticky header with glassmorphism, new Hero with factory background, Trust Bar stats stripe.

### Phase 3 — About + Export Section
Rebuild Discover Pyramids split-layout. Build the brand-new Global Export section.

### Phase 4 — Products + Modal
Rebuild product cards with use-case tags. Enhance modal with size selection, Best Value badge, WhatsApp CTA.

### Phase 5 — Services + Trust Counters + FAQ
Rebuild services grid (6 cards). Add animated stat counters section. Rebuild FAQ as pure CSS accordion.

### Phase 6 — CTA Banner + Contact + Footer
Full-width CTA with WhatsApp button. Rebuild contact form section. Three-column footer.

### Phase 7 — i18n + Mobile + Polish
Update JSON translation files with all new copy. Full mobile responsiveness QA. Micro-animations, hover effects, scroll performance tuning.

---

## Open Questions for Your Review

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Hero Background:** The plan uses `image-13.jpg` (factory photo) as the hero background with a dark gradient overlay. Do you have any additional real adhesive-usage photos you'd like to use instead?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **About Page:** Should `about.html` be a priority in this remake, or do we rebuild only `index.html` first and tackle the about page separately?

> [!WARNING]
> **Bootstrap Removal:** Removing Bootstrap CSS is the cleanest approach for a bespoke design, but means writing our own modal, grid, and accordion from scratch. This is absolutely doable and results in a smaller, faster site. Confirm you're comfortable with this direction.

> [!NOTE]
> **Language Switcher:** The existing i18n JSON files and `language.js` are solid. I plan to carry them forward with new keys added for the new sections. No redesign of the i18n logic is needed.
